From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] login_manager: a NickelOS local account's session runs Chrome
 as its Linux user

A local account (<name>@nickel.localhost, created by nickel-accountsd) is
the Linux user <name> (uid 5000-5999). Once its session has started,
Chrome restarts itself (Chrome patch), and session_manager runs the next
Chrome, and every restart until the session ends, as that user, with USER
and LOGNAME to match. The login screen's Chrome stays chronos.

Chrome creates most of its state outside the vault 0600/0700, so before
each Chrome start the state is handed to the user about to run it: the
contents of /home/chronos (except vault mounts and per-user dirs; the dir
itself stays chronos's, group-writable, as cryptohome requires),
/run/chrome, /var/log/chrome and the other dirs ChromeSetup creates for
Chrome. Only entries owned by chronos or a local account change hands.

ui-pre-start gives group chronos the write access to Chrome's cgroups and
/var/spool/support that chronos has; ui-post-stop ends a local account's
leftover processes the way it ends chronos's.

---
diff -ruN a/login_manager/browser_job.cc b/login_manager/browser_job.cc
